@event duelling_captain_challenge
# en: The Captain's Challenge
title [3e0fbf] = 队长的挑战
# en: {A visiting champion has challenged the Circle's captain, by name, in front of everyone. The captain is you.|Another challenger at the door, asking for the captain.|They come for the captain now, from three valleys away.} {The hall is packed to the rafters.|{around(lyra): Lyra is in the front row with her arms folded.|The old captains are in the front row with their arms folded.}|Somebody is taking bets in the corridor.}
text [616d0c] = {一位来访的冠军当着所有人的面，点名挑战决斗社的队长。队长就是你。|门口又来了一个挑战者，指名要找队长。|如今有人从三个山谷之外赶来挑战队长。}{大厅里挤得水泄不通。|{around(lyra): 莱拉抱着胳膊坐在第一排。|几位前任队长抱着胳膊坐在第一排。}|有人在走廊里坐庄下注。}
# en: A captain of a duelling circle in a chalk ring facing a visiting champion, the whole hall packed to the rafters.
scene [f26cae] = 决斗社的队长站在粉笔圈里，对面是来访的冠军，整个大厅挤得水泄不通。
# en: Accept in front of everyone
opt.left.label [c550e1] = 当着所有人的面应战
# en: {You win the third exchange and the hall comes apart. The champion bows, properly. The Circle will talk about it for a year.|A long, hard bout, and yours at the end. Your name goes on the board in gold paint.|You accept, with bets being taken in the corridor. You win, and somebody in the corridor wins a great deal more.}
opt.left.say.1 [a1e423] = {你在第三回合取胜，整个大厅炸开了锅。冠军郑重地鞠了一躬。决斗社会把这件事谈论一整年。|一场漫长而艰苦的较量，最后是你赢了。你的名字被用金漆写上了荣誉榜。|走廊里有人在下注，你接受了挑战。你赢了，走廊里有人赢得比你多得多。}
# en: {You lose, in front of everyone, by a breath. The Circle carries you to the infirmary anyway, which is its own verdict.|Beaten, cleanly. The champion is gracious. That's the worst part.|You lose to someone from three valleys away, and the corridor pays out. The Circle buys you a drink with the winnings it didn't make.}
opt.left.say.2 [fb3105] = {你当着所有人的面输了，只差一口气。决斗社还是把你抬去了医务室，这本身就是一种评价。|干脆利落地输了。冠军很有风度。这才是最难受的。|你输给了一个从三个山谷外来的人，走廊里的赌局开始赔钱。决斗社用它没赢到的钱请你喝了一杯。}
# en: Send your best officer instead
opt.right.label [50ddb4] = 派你最好的干事上场
# en: {Your officer wins, narrowly, and the hall cheers for the Circle. A few people look at you and wonder why you didn't step up.|You coach from the edge. The officer loses but fights well. It was the right call, you think, mostly.|You send your officer. They win, and the corridor's bookmaker grumbles that the captain was the better bet.}
opt.right.say.1 [fbcd3e] = {你的干事险胜，大厅为决斗社欢呼。有几个人看着你，纳闷你为什么没有亲自上场。|你在场边指导。干事输了，但打得很好。这是正确的决定，你想，大体上是。|你派出了干事。干事赢了，走廊里坐庄的人抱怨说押队长才稳。}

@event duelling_captain_injury
# en: The Captain's Call
title [65921a] = 队长的决定
# en: {A first-year in the Circle has twisted a wrist in the final of the house cup, and insists on finishing.|Another final, another stubborn first-year with an injury.|The house cup final again, and again someone hurt who won't stop.} {The house's honour is riding on it.|Their parents are in the gallery.|The referee looks at you: the captain decides.}
text [d60d62] = {决斗社的一个一年级生在院际杯决赛中扭伤了手腕，却坚持要打完。|又一场决赛，又一个受了伤还不肯下场的一年级生。|又是院际杯决赛，又有人受了伤却不肯停。}{学院的荣誉全押在这一场上。|他们的父母就在看台上。|裁判看向你：由队长决定。}
# en: A duellist kneeling in a chalk circle clutching a wrist, a captain crouching beside them, a referee waiting with a whistle.
scene [89c135] = 一个决斗者跪在粉笔圈里捂着手腕，队长蹲在一旁，裁判拿着哨子等待。
# en: Let them finish
opt.left.label [726d27] = 让他们打完
# en: {They finish, and win, with one hand. The gallery stands. You stood beside them, and you'll remember the fear more than the win.|They finish and win. Amaranth bandages them afterwards and gives you a look that could strip paint.|The referee looks at you, and you nod. They finish, and win, and you hold your breath through every exchange.}
opt.left.say.1 [54b4bf] = {他们用一只手打完了，还赢了。看台上的人全站了起来。你一直站在他们身旁，你记住的会是恐惧，而不是胜利。|他们打完了，赢了。阿玛兰斯修女事后给他们包扎，看你的眼神能刮掉一层漆。|裁判看向你，你点了头。他们打完了，赢了，每一回合你都屏着气。}
# en: {They finish and lose, and the wrist is worse. Sister Amaranth sends for you specifically, to explain.|The bout ends with a second injury. You let it happen. You don't sleep that night.|The referee looks at you, you nod, and you're wrong. The wrist goes. You walk them to the infirmary yourself.}
opt.left.say.2 [2b62e7] = {他们打完了，输了，手腕伤得更重了。阿玛兰斯修女特地派人找你去解释。|这场比赛以第二次受伤告终。是你让它发生的。那天夜里你没有睡着。|裁判看向你，你点了头，可你错了。手腕彻底伤了。你亲自把他们送去了医务室。}
# en: Stop the bout
opt.right.label [484d08] = 叫停比赛
# en: {You call it. The house loses the cup and the first-year cries and calls you a coward. A week later, in the corridor, they thank you.|You stop it. The gallery boos. {around(lyra): Lyra, in the front row, nods once.|The referee, pocketing the whistle, nods once.}|The referee looks at you, and you stop it. The first-year doesn't speak to you for a week, then asks you to coach them.}
opt.right.say.1 [43f5f4] = {你叫停了。学院输掉了奖杯，那个一年级生哭着骂你是懦夫。一个星期后，在走廊里，他们向你道了谢。|你叫停了。看台上一片嘘声。{around(lyra): 第一排的莱拉点了一下头。|裁判把哨子揣回兜里，点了一下头。}|裁判看向你，你叫停了。那个一年级生一个星期没理你，然后来请你当他们的教练。}

@event lumen_ledger_editor_scoop
# en: The Story That Could Close Us
title [202765] = 可能让报社关门的报道
# en: {A reporter brings you a story about a governor of the academy, apparently true and well sourced, and dangerous.|Another story with teeth, on your desk with a dawn deadline.|Nessa calls it "the kind of story that closes papers". She says it admiringly.} {The evidence is a stack of letters.|The source wants to stay unnamed.|The printer needs the pages by dawn.}
text [b5834d] = {一个记者给你带来一篇关于学院一位董事的报道，看上去属实，来源可靠，也很危险。|又一篇带刺的报道摆在你的桌上，天亮前就得付印。|内莎说这是“能让报社关门的那种报道”。她说这话时带着钦佩。}{证据是一叠信件。|消息来源要求匿名。|印刷工天亮前就要版面。}
# en: A cramped newspaper office at night, a student editor reading a draft under a lamp, a stack of evidence beside it and the clock showing late.
scene [4d4f9d] = 夜里一间狭小的报社办公室，一个学生主编在灯下读着稿子，旁边摞着证据，钟表显示已经很晚了。
# en: Run it on the front page
opt.left.label [b4bc4b] = 登上头版
# en: {Every fact holds. The Ledger sells out by breakfast; the governor resigns by supper. Nessa frames the front page.|It runs, it holds, and the castle talks of nothing else for a week.|You run it with the printer waiting, and every fact holds. Nessa says it's the story that closes papers, and it closes someone else's career instead.}
opt.left.say.1 [71ac0c] = {每一个事实都站得住。《流明纪事报》早饭前就卖光了；那位董事晚饭前就辞了职。内莎把那期头版裱了起来。|报道刊出，经得住推敲，整个城堡一个星期都在谈论这件事。|你在印刷工的等待中把它发了出去，每个事实都站得住。内莎说这是能让报纸关门的稿子，结果关门的是别人的前程。}
# en: {One fact was wrong, and it's the one they sue over. The Ledger prints a retraction; you write it. Detention, too, for good measure.|It runs, with a mistake in it. The governor's lawyers are very polite, and very thorough.|You run it by dawn, and the dawn is too soon. One fact needed another day. The retraction is yours to write.}
opt.left.say.2 [acb720] = {有一个事实错了，偏偏就是他们起诉的那一条。《流明纪事报》刊登了更正声明，由你执笔。顺便还有一次禁闭。|报道刊出了，里面有个错误。那位董事的律师们非常有礼貌，也非常彻底。|你赶在黎明前发了稿，可黎明来得太早了。有一个事实还需要多核实一天。更正由你来写。}
# en: Hold it until it's airtight
opt.right.label [145ca0] = 压到万无一失再说
# en: {You hold it. Another paper in the village runs a thinner version first. Nessa doesn't speak to you for two days, then admits you were right.|You hold it for a month and check every line. When it finally runs, it's bulletproof, and old news.|You hold the presses until it's airtight. The printer charges you for the dawn, and Nessa pays it, grumbling.}
opt.right.say.1 [af6116] = {你压下了稿子。村里另一家报纸先登了一个单薄的版本。内莎两天没跟你说话，然后承认你是对的。|你压了一个月，每一行都核实过。等它终于刊出，已经无懈可击，也已经是旧闻了。|你压住印刷机，直到稿子无懈可击。印刷工为这个黎明收了你的钱，内莎嘟囔着付了。}

@event lumen_ledger_editor_threat
# en: A Letter to the Editor
title [2a57e7] = 致编辑的信
# en: {A letter to the editor, unsigned, about a story you ran. It knows where you sleep.|Another unsigned letter, the same careful hand.|The letters have stopped being polite.} {It smells of expensive ink.|The seal has been scraped off.|It's been slipped under the office door, not posted.}
text [e93e25] = {一封致编辑的匿名信，针对你刊出的一篇报道。它知道你睡在哪儿。|又一封匿名信，同样工整的笔迹。|这些信已经不再客气了。}{它闻起来是昂贵墨水的味道。|火漆印被刮掉了。|它是从编辑部门缝底下塞进来的，不是寄来的。}
# en: A black-edged letter open on a newspaper desk, a student editor reading it with a cold face, the window behind them dark.
scene [34ca74] = 一封黑边信摊在报社的桌上，一个学生主编面色冰冷地读着，身后的窗户一片漆黑。
# en: Print it, with a reply
opt.left.label [0cd1a2] = 登出来，附上回应
# en: {You print it in full on page two, with three lines of your own beneath. The castle loves it. You check your door twice every night for a month.|The letter goes in the paper. The next one takes a month to come. The waiting for it is worse.|You print the impolite one, impolitely answered. The letters stop. You don't know whether that's good.}
opt.left.say.1 [185ef7] = {你把它全文登在第二版，下面附上你自己的三行字。全城堡都爱看。接下来一个月，你每晚都要检查两遍门。|信登在了报纸上。下一封隔了一个月才来。等它的滋味更难受。|你把那封不客气的信登了出来，也不客气地回了。信不再来了。你不知道这是好是坏。}
# en: Take it to the headmistress
opt.right.label [069089] = 交给校长
# en: {She reads it once and puts it in a drawer. "Leave it with me." For a long while, you don't get another. Nessa says that's censorship. It's also sleep.|The headmistress handles it. You don't ask how. The Ledger is quieter for a while.|The headmistress reads the one slipped under the door and asks who has a key to the office. The locks are changed by evening.}
opt.right.say.1 [24b851] = {她读了一遍就把信放进了抽屉。“交给我吧。”很长一段时间里，你没再收到过。内莎说这是审查。这也是能睡个好觉。|校长处理了这件事。你没问她怎么处理的。《流明纪事报》安静了一阵子。|院长读了那封塞在门下的信，问谁有编辑部的钥匙。傍晚之前锁就换了。}

@event verdant_head_gardener_blight
# en: The Blight
title [b7ffa6] = 枯萎病
# en: {Blight in the greenhouses, black spots spreading by the hour. The Head Gardener decides what to burn.|The blight is back, in a different house.|Black spots again. You know the smell of it now.} {{around(tobias): Tobias is close to tears.|The Circle's youngest member is close to tears.}|The rarest plant in the collection is at the edge of it.|Maud has come up from the cottage to look.}
text [a2f41a] = {温室里闹起了枯萎病，黑斑一小时一小时地蔓延。首席园丁决定烧掉什么。|枯萎病又来了，在另一间温室。|又是黑斑。你现在已经熟悉它的气味了。}{{around(tobias): 托比亚斯快哭了。|社里年纪最小的成员快哭了。}|收藏里最稀有的那株植物就在病区边上。|莫德从小屋上来看了。}
# en: A greenhouse full of wilting plants, black spots on every leaf, a head gardener holding a sickly seedling up to the light.
scene [5e45ab] = 一间满是枯萎植物的温室，每片叶子上都有黑斑，一个首席园丁把一株病恹恹的幼苗举到光下。
# en: Try an untested cure on everything
opt.left.label [ee10e0] = 在所有植物上试一种未经检验的疗法
# en: {The cure works, overnight. Every plant lives, even the rare one. Maud says she's never seen it done, and asks for the recipe.|By morning the spots are fading. The Circle sings, badly, in the greenhouse.|Maud watches you try the cure and says nothing until it works. Then she asks for the recipe, and you give it.}
opt.left.say.1 [3b609d] = {疗法一夜见效。每一株都活了下来，连那株稀有的也是。莫德说她从没见过有人做到，还向你要了配方。|到了早上，黑斑渐渐褪去。青翠社的人在温室里唱起了歌，唱得很难听。|莫德看着你试那个疗法，一直没说话，直到它见效。然后她向你要配方，你给了。}
# en: {The cure kills what the blight hadn't. You burn the whole house. {around(tobias): Tobias helps|The Circle helps}, and nobody blames you, which is worse.|It fails. You lose half the collection, and all of your confidence for a week.|Maud watches the cure fail and helps you burn what's left. "Everyone loses a house once," she says. "Once."}
opt.left.say.2 [f0aeea] = {疗法杀死了枯萎病没杀死的东西。你烧掉了整间温室。{around(tobias): 托比亚斯来帮忙|社员们来帮忙}，谁也没有怪你，这更难受。|失败了。你失去了一半的收藏，还有整整一个星期的自信。|莫德看着疗法失败，帮你把剩下的烧了。“谁都会丢一间温室，”她说，“一次。”}
# en: Burn the sick plants now
opt.right.label [90fc07] = 现在就烧掉病株
# en: {You burn a third of the house and save the rest. It's the right call and it smells of grief.|You burn the sick ones before it spreads. The rare plant is among them.|Maud nods at what you burn and points at one plant you missed. You burn that too. She was right.}
opt.right.say.1 [051d3a] = {你烧掉了三分之一的温室，保住了其余的。这是正确的决定，闻起来却像悲伤。|你在它蔓延之前烧掉了病株。那株稀有的也在其中。|莫德对你烧掉的那些点点头，又指了指一株你漏掉的。你把那株也烧了。她是对的。}

@event verdant_head_gardener_show
# en: The Valley Fair
title [a34a57] = 山谷集市
# en: {The valley's flower show, and the Verdant Circle's entry is yours to choose.|The flower show again; the judges remember you.|The show tent smells of crushed grass and rivalry.} {A farmer's pumpkin is the size of a cart.|Thornwick has sent a team.|The judges are three old women who have seen everything.}
text [6fe4b1] = {山谷里的花展到了，青翠社的参展作品由你来选。|又是花展；评委们还记得你。|展棚里弥漫着压碎的青草味和较劲的味道。}{一个农夫的南瓜有一辆车那么大。|荆木学院派了一支队伍来。|评委是三位见多识广的老太太。}
# en: A crowded show tent in a village field, prize vegetables on trestle tables, a student head gardener carrying an enormous potted plant toward the judges.
scene [1ae86c] = 村里田野上一座拥挤的展棚，搁板桌上摆着获奖的蔬菜，一个学生首席园丁捧着一盆巨大的植物走向评委。
# en: Enter the night-blooming lily
opt.left.label [0b838e] = 送夜开百合参展
# en: {It opens at dusk in front of the judges, as if on cue. First prize, and a purse, and a drawing in the village paper.|The lily wins, narrowly, over a cabbage. Nobody will forget the cabbage's grower's face.|The three old judges watch the lily open and say nothing. Then all three write "first" at once.}
opt.left.say.1 [3e17d0] = {黄昏时它在评委面前绽放，仿佛算准了时机。头奖，一袋奖金，还有村报上的一幅插画。|百合以微弱优势胜过了一颗卷心菜。没人会忘记那位卷心菜种植者的表情。|三位老评委看着百合绽放，一言不发。然后三个人同时写下了“第一”。}
# en: {It refuses to open. The cabbage wins. The lily blooms at midnight, for nobody, in your arms.|Second place, to Thornwick. {around(tobias): Tobias says|The Circle says} second is good. It isn't.|The three old judges have seen night-blooming lilies before. They give it a polite second and the cabbage a ribbon.}
opt.left.say.2 [add267] = {它不肯开。卷心菜赢了。百合在午夜绽放，只为你一个人，在你怀里。|第二名，输给了荆木学院。{around(tobias): 托比亚斯说|社员们说}第二名也很好。并不好。|那三位老评委以前就见过夜开的百合。她们礼貌地给了它第二名，给了卷心菜一条绶带。}
# en: Enter the reliable roses
opt.right.label [3ae698] = 送稳妥的玫瑰参展
# en: {Third prize for the roses. Solid, respectable, forgettable.|The roses place. The Circle is pleased; the Circle is also bored.|The three old judges approve of roses. Second prize, and a long talk about pruning you'll actually use.}
opt.right.say.1 [3995c0] = {玫瑰拿了第三名。扎实，体面，转眼就忘。|玫瑰得了名次。青翠社很满意；青翠社也很无聊。|那三位老评委喜欢玫瑰。第二名，外加一席关于修剪的长谈，你还真用得上。}

@event library_senior_banned_book
# en: A Request for a Banned Book
title [5026f0] = 借阅禁书的请求
# en: {A first-year brings you a request slip for a chained book. Senior clerks hold the keys, and the rules say no.|Another request for a chained book, from a student who looks desperate.|They've heard you hold the keys. The slips keep coming.} {The first-year's essay depends on it.|The slip is signed by a professor, perhaps.|The book in question bites.}
text [775ce5] = {一个一年级生递来一张借书单，要借一本上了锁链的书。钥匙在资深馆员手里，规矩说不行。|又一张借锁链书的单子，借书的学生看起来走投无路。|他们听说钥匙在你手里。借书单一张接一张地来。}{那个一年级生的作业全靠这本书了。|借书单上有一位教授的签名，大概吧。|那本书会咬人。}
# en: A library desk at closing time, a nervous first-year holding a request slip for a chained book, a senior clerk with the keys looking down at it.
scene [c4f362] = 闭馆时分的图书馆服务台，一个紧张的一年级生拿着借锁链书的单子，一个拿着钥匙的资深馆员低头看着它。
# en: Fetch it, against the rules
opt.left.label [b72eb7] = 违规去取
# en: {You fetch it, watch them read it, and chain it back before closing. Nobody knows. The first-year passes with honours and leaves you a cake with crowns folded under it.|The book goes out and comes back, with a grateful envelope. The rules bent, and didn't break.|You fetch it in gloves. It bites the glove and not the reader. The essay is excellent, and the glove is a loss.}
opt.left.say.1 [527293] = {你取来书，看着他们读完，闭馆前再锁回去。没人知道。那个一年级生以优异成绩通过，给你留了一块蛋糕，底下压着几枚克朗。|书借出去又还回来，附带一个表示感谢的信封。规矩弯了，没断。|你戴着手套去取。它咬了手套，没咬读者。论文写得很出色，手套报废了。}
# en: {The head librarian finds the chain unlocked. Half your pay docked and a long, quiet talk.|Caught, with the key in your hand, and docked for it. You're still Senior Clerk; nobody quite knows how.|It bites the reader, and the head librarian sees the bandage. Your pay is docked, and the reader's thanks are muffled.}
opt.left.say.2 [289a6c] = {总馆员发现锁链开着。扣了一半的工钱，外加一场长长的、安静的谈话。|被抓了个正着，钥匙还在你手里，工钱也因此被扣。你仍然是资深馆员；没人说得清这是怎么回事。|它咬了读者，总馆员看见了绷带。你的工钱被扣了，读者的道谢也说得含含糊糊。}
# en: Refuse
opt.right.label [cada35] = 拒绝
# en: {You say no. The first-year leaves in tears. The head librarian, who heard, nods.|The rules hold. So does your conscience, more or less.|You say no, and show them the book from a safe distance. They see it snap at the air and stop asking.}
opt.right.say.1 [d33e92] = {你说了不。那个一年级生哭着走了。听到这番话的总馆员点了点头。|规矩守住了。你的良心也大致守住了。|你说了不，然后隔着安全距离让他们看了看那本书。他们看见它对着空气咬了一口，就不再求了。}

@event library_senior_night_flood
# en: Water in the Stacks
title [ccea75] = 书库进水
# en: {A pipe bursts in the lower stacks at the end of your shift, and the senior clerk on duty is you.|Water in the stacks again. The pipes are older than the books.|The lower level floods every spring now.} {The rarest books are on the bottom shelf.|The water is rising.|Someone is shouting for help two floors up.}
text [1c6040] = {你的班快结束时，下层书库的一根水管爆了，当值的资深馆员就是你。|书库又进水了。这些水管比书还老。|如今下层每年春天都要淹。}{最稀有的书就在最底层的书架上。|水在上涨。|楼上两层有人在喊救命。}
# en: A flooded lower library level at night, water lapping at the bottom shelves, a senior clerk wading with an armful of books.
scene [58c52c] = 夜里被淹的图书馆下层，水拍打着最底层的书架，一个资深馆员抱着一摞书蹚水而行。
# en: Save the rare books first
opt.left.label [e4b589] = 先抢救稀有的书
# en: {You carry armful after armful up the stair in freezing water until long after closing. Every rare book saved. Your boots are not.|You save the rarest and lose the common ones, and the head librarian, arriving at last, hugs you, which nobody has ever seen.|You save the rare books and then go up for the shouting. It's a first-year stuck on a ladder. You save them too.}
opt.left.say.1 [02e465] = {你在冰冷的水里一趟又一趟地把书抱上楼梯，一直忙到闭馆后很久。每一本稀有的书都保住了。你的靴子没保住。|你救下了最稀有的，丢掉了普通的，总馆员终于赶到，抱了抱你，这是谁都没见过的事。|你救下了稀有的书，又上楼去找那个喊叫的人。是个困在梯子上的一年级生。你把对方也救了下来。}
# en: Run for the head librarian
opt.right.label [ffaf08] = 跑去找总馆员
# en: {By the time she comes, a shelf is lost. "You did right to fetch me," she says, and looks at the shelf.|She takes charge. You carry what she points at.|You run for the head librarian, past the shouting two floors up. She sends you back for the shouter first. She was right.}
opt.right.say.1 [100588] = {等她赶到时，一整架书已经毁了。“你去找我是对的，”她说，看着那架书。|她接手指挥。她指什么，你就搬什么。|你跑去找总馆员，路过两层楼上的呼喊声。她让你先回去救喊叫的人。她是对的。}

@event tavern_manager_inspector
# en: The Inspector Calls
title [663f74] = 检查员来访
# en: {The licensing inspector is here, unannounced, and the landlady is away. The manager is you.|The inspector again, with the same long coat and longer list.|The inspector nods at you like an old enemy.} {The cellar has a leak.|The ledger has a page you'd rather they didn't read.|There's a goblin asleep in the back booth.}
text [69f885] = {执照检查员不打招呼就来了，老板娘不在。经理就是你。|又是那位检查员，同样的长大衣，更长的清单。|检查员像对老冤家一样冲你点点头。}{地窖漏水。|账簿里有一页你宁愿他们别看。|后面的卡座里睡着一个地精。}
# en: A village tavern in the morning, a stern inspector in a long coat running a finger along a bar, a student manager following with a ledger.
scene [3c5a55] = 早上的村酒馆，一个穿长大衣的严厉检查员用手指抹过吧台，一个学生经理拿着账簿跟在后面。
# en: Show everything, honestly
opt.left.label [cf598d] = 老老实实地全部展示
# en: {The inspector finds the leak, notes it and passes the Newt with a warning. The landlady, back, gives you a bonus and her late mother's tankard.|A clean bill, almost. The inspector shakes your hand.|The inspector finds the goblin in the back booth, who turns out to be licensed. A clean bill, and a very long afternoon.}
opt.left.say.1 [c08744] = {检查员发现了漏水，记了下来，给了蝾螈酒馆一个警告就放行了。老板娘回来后给了你一笔奖金，还有她已故母亲的那只大酒杯。|几乎干干净净。检查员和你握了握手。|检查员在后面的卡座里发现了那个地精，结果对方有执照。检查通过，下午也过得很漫长。}
# en: {The fine is steep, the landlady takes a share out of your wages, and her face is steeper.|Three infractions. The till covers most of the fine. Your own wages cover the rest.|The inspector wakes the goblin in the back booth, who has opinions about inspectors. The fine is for the opinions.}
opt.left.say.2 [7b7778] = {罚款很重，老板娘从你的工钱里扣了一份，她的脸色更重。|三项违规。钱柜付了大部分罚款，剩下的由你的工钱来付。|检查员吵醒了后面卡座里的地精，对方对检查员很有意见。罚款罚的就是这些意见。}
# en: Steer them away from the cellar
opt.right.label [666330] = 引他们避开地窖
# en: {The inspector never goes downstairs. You fix the leak that night with your own hands, guiltily.|A clean bill, by omission. You don't tell the landlady how.|You steer the inspector past the back booth and the goblin sleeps on. A clean bill, by the narrowest of margins.}
opt.right.say.1 [aae7bf] = {检查员始终没下楼。那天夜里你亲手修好了漏水，心里有愧。|靠隐瞒换来的干净。你没告诉老板娘是怎么做到的。|你引着检查员绕过后面的卡座，地精继续睡。检查通过，险之又险。}
# en: {The inspector goes straight to the cellar. The fine doubles for "obstruction". Bram hears of it somehow.|Caught steering. The inspector writes your name down in a separate book.|The goblin in the back booth wakes and gives the inspector a tour. Of the cellar.}
opt.right.say.2 [68e7ad] = {检查员径直走向地窖。罚款因为“妨碍检查”翻了一倍。布拉姆不知怎么听说了。|你引路被识破了。检查员把你的名字记在另一个本子上。|后面卡座里的地精醒了，热情地带检查员参观。参观的是地窖。}

@event tavern_manager_grisk_offer
# en: An Investor
title [49ae9a] = 一位投资人
# en: {Grisk would like to invest in the Newt, with new chairs and a second fire, "and a little room upstairs for my associates".|Grisk again, with a bigger bag of coin.|"My offer stands," says Grisk, "and grows."} {The chairs really are falling apart.|The landlady is away.|The bag of coin is very heavy.}
text [329733] = {格里斯克想投资蝾螈酒馆，新椅子，再加一个壁炉，“还有楼上给我的合伙人留个小房间”。|又是格里斯克，钱袋更大了。|“我的提议依然有效，”格里斯克说，“而且还在加码。”}{那些椅子确实快散架了。|老板娘不在。|那袋钱非常沉。}
# en: A goblin in a velvet waistcoat sitting at a tavern's best table, a bag of coin and a contract in front of him, a student manager standing opposite.
scene [dbb834] = 一个穿天鹅绒马甲的地精坐在酒馆最好的桌子旁，面前放着一袋钱和一份合同，一个学生经理站在对面。
# en: Take his money for the chairs
opt.left.label [e60668] = 收下他的钱换椅子
# en: {New chairs, a second fire, a fat "manager's commission" in your pocket, and Grisk's associates upstairs on Thursdays. Trade is up. So is the noise, at midnight.|Grisk pays you a finder's cut in a sealed envelope. The Newt has never looked better. The upstairs room has never been busier, and you don't go up there.|You take the heavy bag. Grisk's offer grows into the upstairs, then the cellar, then your evenings. The commission is excellent.}
opt.left.say.1 [797c9a] = {新椅子，第二个壁炉，你口袋里一笔丰厚的“经理佣金”，每周四楼上坐着格里斯克的合伙人。生意好了。午夜的吵闹也多了。|格里斯克用一个封好的信封付了你一笔介绍费。蝾螈酒馆从没这么气派过。楼上的房间从没这么热闹过，而你从不上去。|你收下了那只沉甸甸的钱袋。格里斯克的投资从楼上扩展到地窖，再到你的晚上。佣金非常可观。}
# en: Turn him down
opt.right.label [b56858] = 拒绝他
# en: {"Your loss," says Grisk, and means it as a threat. The chairs stay wobbly.|You say no. Grisk tips his hat and drinks somewhere else for a month, which hurts trade.|You turn the heavier bag down too. Grisk laughs, and says he likes a manager with standards. He'll be back.}
opt.right.say.1 [d2cba7] = {“你的损失，”格里斯克说，这话是威胁。椅子还是摇摇晃晃。|你说了不。格里斯克抬了抬帽子，去别处喝了一个月，生意受了影响。|你连更沉的那只钱袋也拒绝了。格里斯克笑了，说他喜欢有原则的经理。他还会再来。}

@event apothecary_assistant_poison
# en: A Dangerous Prescription
title [08b2dc] = 危险的处方
# en: {A prescription comes in from a village healer with a dose ten times too strong. Pell is out. Assistant apothecaries decide.|Another slip with a strange dose. You've learned to read the healer's handwriting, which doesn't help.|A dose that would fell a horse, for an old shepherd.} {The patient's grown son is waiting.|The healer is a day's ride away.|It might be a slip of the pen. It might not.}
text [89141c] = {村里一位治疗师送来一张处方，剂量重了十倍。佩尔不在。由助理药师决定。|又一张剂量古怪的单子。你已经认得那位治疗师的字迹了，可这没用。|能放倒一匹马的剂量，开给一个老牧羊人。}{病人已成年的儿子在等着。|治疗师在一天的路程之外。|可能是笔误。也可能不是。}
# en: An apothecary counter, a prescription slip with a dose underlined in red, a young assistant alone behind the counter frowning at it.
scene [ac1da0] = 药铺柜台上一张处方，剂量下面画着红线，一位年轻的助理独自站在柜台后，皱眉看着它。
# en: Mix it at a safe dose
opt.left.label [bc845e] = 按安全剂量调配
# en: {You work out what the healer meant and mix that. The patient recovers. Pell, back, reads the slip and goes white, then pats your shoulder for a long time.|Right dose, right remedy. The healer writes later to thank you, embarrassed.|You mix the shepherd a dose that wouldn't fell a sparrow. It works. The healer, told, sends Pell a very apologetic letter.}
opt.left.say.1 [98b4d0] = {你推断出治疗师的本意，按那个剂量调了药。病人好了。佩尔回来看了那张单子，脸都白了，然后拍了你的肩膀很久。|剂量对，药也对。治疗师后来写信道谢，很是难为情。|你给那位牧羊人调了一剂连麻雀都撂不倒的药。管用了。治疗师听说后，给佩尔写了一封非常抱歉的信。}
# en: {Your safe dose is too weak. The patient recovers slowly, and the son tells the whole village.|You get it nearly right. Nearly is a word you stop using for a while.|You cut the dose so far that it does nothing. The shepherd comes back, unwell, and Pell has to sort it out.}
opt.left.say.2 [2abb4d] = {你的安全剂量太弱了。病人好得很慢，他儿子告诉了全村。|你差不多调对了。有一阵子你不再用“差不多”这个词。|你把剂量减得太多，毫无作用。牧羊人又回来了，还是不舒服，佩尔只好亲自处理。}
# en: Refuse until the healer confirms
opt.right.label [14e4f0] = 等治疗师确认后再说
# en: {A day's wait. The patient's son shouts at you. The healer confirms the slip was wrong. You were right, and it was a long day.|You send a rider. The answer comes at midnight. You stay up for it.|It was a slip of the pen. The healer confirms by midnight, and you mix the right dose by one.}
opt.right.say.1 [b2d046] = {等了一天。病人的儿子冲你大喊大叫。治疗师确认单子写错了。你是对的，那是漫长的一天。|你派人骑马去问。答复半夜才到。你一直等着。|那是笔误。治疗师午夜前确认了，你一点前调好了正确的剂量。}

@event apothecary_assistant_rival_shop
# en: A Shop Across the Square
title [3596c9] = 广场对面的铺子
# en: {A new apothecary has opened across the square, all brass and bright bottles and half Pell's prices.|The shop across the square has a queue now.|Pell has started calling the new shop "that brass insult".} {Their remedies are mostly coloured water.|They've hired a singer for the doorway.|Pell's daughters have written to ask what's wrong.}
text [e6dd15] = {广场对面新开了一家药铺，满眼铜器和亮闪闪的瓶子，价钱只有佩尔的一半。|广场对面的铺子现在排起了队。|佩尔开始管那家新铺子叫“那个铜皮侮辱”。}{他们的药大多是染了色的水。|他们雇了个歌手站在门口。|佩尔的女儿们写信来问出了什么事。}
# en: A gleaming new apothecary shop across a village square, its window full of bright bottles, an old apothecary peering at it from his own doorway.
scene [1729f3] = 村广场对面一家闪亮的新药铺，橱窗里满是亮闪闪的瓶子，一位老药师从自家门口朝那边张望。
# en: Expose their coloured water
opt.left.label [4016d1] = 揭穿他们的染色水
# en: {You buy a bottle of everything and test them in Pell's back room. The results go on a board in the window. The brass shop closes by the season's end.|Your tests are fair and public. The village comes back to Pell, a little sheepish.|You write to Pell's daughters with your test results. They come home for a week and help you nail the board to the window.}
opt.left.say.1 [a4b64a] = {你把他们的每样药都买了一瓶，在佩尔的后屋里检验。结果贴在橱窗的告示板上。那家铜器铺子没到季末就关门了。|你的检验公平又公开。村里人回到了佩尔这儿，有点不好意思。|你把检验结果写信告诉了佩尔的女儿们。她们回来住了一个星期，帮你把告示板钉到了橱窗上。}
# en: {Their remedies turn out to work, annoyingly. You look petty. Pell says, "Well, now we know."|Inconclusive, and everyone saw you try.|Pell's daughters write back that the brass shop's remedies are fine and that you should worry about Pell's. You do.}
opt.left.say.2 [a8d769] = {偏偏他们的药是管用的。你显得小家子气。佩尔说：“好吧，现在我们知道了。”|没有定论，而且所有人都看见你试过了。|佩尔的女儿们回信说铜器铺子的药没问题，你该担心的是佩尔的药。你开始担心了。}
# en: Lower Pell's prices
opt.right.label [8b354b] = 降低佩尔的价钱
# en: {Cheaper remedies, longer hours, a full shop. Pell grumbles and is secretly delighted.|You match them on price and beat them on care. It's slow, and it works.|You lower the prices and write to the daughters that all is well. It is, nearly. Pell reads your letter over your shoulder and doesn't object.}
opt.right.say.1 [fd517c] = {更便宜的药，更长的营业时间，满满一铺子人。佩尔嘴上抱怨，心里暗暗高兴。|你在价钱上追平他们，在用心上胜过他们。很慢，但管用。|你降了价，写信告诉女儿们一切都好。差不多算好。佩尔在你肩后读了信，没有反对。}

@event courier_chief_urgent_crossing
# en: The Urgent Crossing
title [50b65f] = 紧急穿越
# en: {A red-sealed package for the far side of the mountains, by tomorrow, and only the chief courier flies red seals.|Another red seal, another gale over the pass.|The red seals come to you by name now.} {The pass is in cloud.|A storm is coming in from the west.|The package is humming.}
text [d958a7] = {一个盖着红色火漆的包裹，明天要送到山那边，只有首席信使能送红漆件。|又一个红漆件，山口上又是一阵大风。|如今红漆件都指名给你。}{山口被云遮住了。|一场风暴正从西边过来。|包裹在嗡嗡作响。}
# en: A courier on a broom flying through a mountain pass in a gale, a red-sealed package clutched to their chest, lightning on the peaks.
scene [75ad0b] = 一个骑着飞帚的信使在大风中穿过山口，怀里紧抱着一个红漆包裹，山峰上电闪雷鸣。
# en: Fly the pass tonight
opt.left.label [8a3c7b] = 今晚就飞过山口
# en: {Through the pass in the dark, lightning on both sides. You deliver at dawn to a pale woman who breaks the seal and weeps with relief. The bonus is the biggest of your life.|You make it, frozen, at dawn. The recipient signs with shaking hands.|The humming package hums louder in the pass and the wind stays off you. You deliver at dawn and don't ask what it was.}
opt.left.say.1 [15256d] = {你在黑暗中穿过山口，两侧都是闪电。天亮时你把包裹交给一个脸色苍白的女人，她拆开火漆，如释重负地哭了。这是你一生中最大的一笔奖金。|你冻僵了，天亮时赶到。收件人签字时双手发抖。|那个嗡嗡作响的包裹在山口里响得更大声，风一直没扑到你身上。你天亮时送到了，没问那是什么。}
# en: {The gale takes you into a snowfield. You walk the last mile with the package and a broken wrist, and arrive late.|You crash short of the pass and are found by a goatherd. The package arrives a day late, via goat.|The humming package hums a note the lightning likes. You land hard and walk it in, late, with the hair on your arms standing up.}
opt.left.say.2 [c99d6d] = {大风把你卷进了雪原。你带着包裹和一只断了的手腕走完最后一英里，到得晚了。|你在山口前坠落，被一个牧羊人发现。包裹晚到了一天，是羊驮去的。|那个嗡嗡作响的包裹哼出了一个闪电喜欢的音。你重重落地，走着把它送到，晚了，胳膊上的汗毛全竖着。}
# en: Wait for the storm to pass
opt.right.label [fd0d0f] = 等风暴过去
# en: {You wait out the storm and fly at dawn. A day late. The recipient is gracious, and the loft-master isn't.|Late but whole. You'll always wonder what was in it.|You wait out the storm with the humming package on the table. It hums all night. You don't sleep.}
opt.right.say.1 [676ccb] = {你等风暴过去，天亮才飞。晚了一天。收件人很宽厚，阁楼主管可不。|晚了，但人是完整的。你会一直好奇里面装的是什么。|你等着暴风雨过去，那个嗡嗡作响的包裹就放在桌上。它哼了一整夜。你没睡着。}

@event courier_chief_new_runner
# en: The New Runner
title [c54f90] = 新来的跑腿
# en: {The loft has a new runner, younger than you were, who holds the broom like a mop.|Another new runner, another bad grip.|The new runners all ask for you now.} {Their first route is across the lake.|They've never flown in rain.|Their parents are watching from the gate.}
text [fcaa4e] = {阁楼来了个新跑腿，比你当年还小，握飞帚像握拖把。|又一个新跑腿，又一个错误的握法。|如今新跑腿们都点名要你带。}{他们的第一条路线要飞过湖。|他们从没在雨里飞过。|他们的父母在门口看着。}
# en: A courier loft at dawn, a nervous young runner holding a broom the wrong way round, a chief courier showing them the grip.
scene [7eddf7] = 清晨的信使阁楼，一个紧张的年轻跑腿把飞帚拿反了，一位首席信使在教他们怎么握。
# en: Fly their first route with them
opt.left.label [03c8ff] = 陪他们飞第一条路线
# en: {You fly beside them across the lake, calling the wind. They land shaking and grinning. They'll name a broom after you, they say.|A slow route, flown twice. They'll be good, one day.|You fly their first route with their parents watching from the gate. They land perfectly and pretend it was nothing.}
opt.left.say.1 [6979fa] = {你在他们身边飞过湖面，替他们喊出风向。他们落地时发着抖，咧着嘴笑。他们说要用你的名字给飞帚命名。|一条慢悠悠的路线，飞了两遍。他们总有一天会飞得很好。|他们的父母在门口看着，你陪他们飞了第一条路线。他们落得完美无缺，还装作若无其事。}
# en: Let them learn on their own
opt.right.label [4c5eb3] = 让他们自己学
# en: {They come back soaked and late, with every parcel. You were the same.|They learn the hard way. So did you.|You let them go alone with their parents watching. They wobble, recover, and wave to the gate. You breathe again.}
opt.right.say.1 [8df8f9] = {他们回来时浑身湿透，晚了，但每个包裹都送到了。你当年也一样。|他们吃了苦头才学会。你也是。|你让他们在父母的注视下独自出发。他们晃了晃，稳住了，朝门口挥手。你这才又喘过气来。}
